{"id":"u-fefd5a87-3f1f-4913-892a-cb398a0696bf","src":"community","title":"POWERBUILDING 12 | Strength & Size","author":"Filip P.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/K5blgV-untitled-program","desc":"POWERBUILDING 12 — Strength & Size\n\nA 12-week, 6-day Push/Pull/Legs program designed to build serious strength and muscle mass through progressive overload, structured periodization, and hypertrophy-focused accessory training.\n\nPROGRAM GOALS\n\n* Increase strength in the squat, bench press, and deadlift.\n* Maximize chest, shoulder, back, and arm development.\n* Build a stronger, more muscular physique.\n* Improve body composition while maintaining lower-body strength.\n\nWEEKLY SPLIT\n\n* Day 1: Push A — Bench Strength\n* Day 2: Pull A — Back Strength\n* Day 3: Legs A — Squat Strength\n* Day 4: Rest\n* Day 5: Push B — Bench Volume & OHP\n* Day 6: Pull B — Back Hypertrophy\n* Day 7: Legs B — Deadlift Strength\n\n12-WEEK PROGRESSION\n\n* Weeks 1–2: Reconditioning and technique.\n* Weeks 3–4: Strength rebuilding and gradual volume increase.\n* Weeks 5–7: Full training volume and progressive overload.\n* Week 8: Deload and recovery.\n* Weeks 9–11: Strength intensification and hypertrophy.\n* Week 12: Performance assessment and rep PRs.\n\nTRAINING PRINCIPLES\n\nHeavy compound movements prioritize strength development, while accessory exercises target muscle hypertrophy.\n\nMain lifts use RPE-based progression. Accessory movements use double progression, increasing repetitions before adding weight.\n\nStart with reduced training volume during the first four weeks and progressively increase training demands as recovery improves.\n\nTrain hard, prioritize technique, track your lifts, and aim for consistent long-term progression.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-14T22:10:35.342Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Push 1","Pull 1","Legs 1","Pu